   "text": {
    "L1": "The poem speaks directly to soldiers. It sounds like a thank-you letter.",
    "L2": "While we sleep warm, soldiers stand on snow in the cold moonlight.",
    "L3": "This contrast shows their hardship and our comfort. Their guarding keeps us safe.",
    "L4": "Our festivals glow and our kites fly free because soldiers guard our land and sea.",
    "L5": "So the central idea is gratitude: we live safely and celebrate because they protect us.",
    "L6": "Say it correctly: we are grateful to our soldiers for guarding our country.",
    "L7": "Here is an apostrophe check. One soldier's boots use 'soldier's'; soldiers marched uses no apostrophe.",
    "L8": "The poem carries feeling, not just description. It thanks the soldiers for their service."
   },
